## Prevention

Four changes, roughly in order of value.

**Alert on the SKI/AKI mismatch directly.** This is the check that would have caught it on day one, and it is cheap — compare the AKI of the certificate in `vault-ha-tls` against the SKI of the CA in `vault-ca-secret` and alert when they diverge. Expiry monitoring would not have helped; the certificate had five weeks left.

**Alert on `VaultClientConfigError`.** The event fired over 34,000 times across 40+ hours and reached nobody. Any Vault client config error sustained beyond a few minutes should page.

**Eliminate hardcoded CA copies.** Every consumer should reference `vault-ca-secret` rather than hold a pasted bundle — `caProvider` for ESO, `caCertSecret` for VSO. The dev mgmt hub ClusterSecretStore proves this works. Where a copy is genuinely unavoidable, it needs an owner and a rotation runbook entry.

**Make CA rotation reissue its leaves.** Nothing currently forces dependent certificates to be reissued when their issuer is replaced. Until that exists, CA rotation needs a manual step: delete `vault-ha-tls`, verify the new AKI, SIGHUP both pods, and update every hardcoded copy in the same window.

The renewal on 27 November will reproduce this exact failure for anything still holding a copy. That is the deadline for the third and fourth items.
